wanted to dissociate himself, and his insistence on the inner religious life of ...\",\"url\":\"https://people.bu.edu/wwildman/bce/mwt_themes_410_pietism.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"104\",\"title\":\"[PDF] John Wesley - Revival and Revolution - Christian History \u0026 Biography\",\"description\":\"At John Wesley׳s death in 1791 his followers numbered 79,000 in England and 40,000 in America, but by 1957 there were 40 million Methodists world-wide!\",\"url\":\"https://christianhistoryinstitute.org/uploaded/50b77f4ed6bbc7.29263299.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"105\",\"title\":\"George Whitefield: Evangelist of the Great Awakening\",\"description\":\"Feb 8, 2018 · His traveling efforts also helped to make the colonies more interconnected and unified in their beliefs and values.\",\"url\":\"https://americanheritage.org/george-whitefield-evangelist-of-the-great-awakening/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"106\",\"title\":\"The First Great Awakening, Divining America, TeacherServe ...\",\"description\":\"The first Great Awakening can best be described as a revitalization of religious piety that swept through the American colonies between the 1730s and the 1770s.\",\"url\":\"https://nationalhumanitiescenter.org/tserve/eighteen/ekeyinfo/grawaken.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"107\",\"title\":\"The First Great Awakening - Timeline Event\",\"description\":\"The First Great Awakening (1733-1770) transformed religious life, aiming for a vital relationship with Christ, with George Whitfield as a prominent figure.\",\"url\":\"https://www.thearda.com/us-religion/history/timelines/entry?etype=1\u0026eid=324\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"108\",\"title\":\"The Second Great Awakening (1800-1835) | United States History I\",\"description\":\"The Second Great Awakening brought significant changes to American culture. Church membership doubled in the years between 1800 and 1835. Several new groups ...\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/wm-ushistory1/chapter/the-second-great-awakening/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"109\",\"title\":\"[PDF] thesecond great awakening - and reform in the 19th century\",\"description\":\"Like the First Great Awakening of the 1730s and 1740s, the. Second Great Awakening emphasized the importance of converting people to Protestant Christianity.\",\"url\":\"https://teachdemocracy.org/wp-content/uploads/2025/07/the-second-great-awakening.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"110\",\"title\":\"Why Did the 1800s Explode with Missions? - Christianity Today\",\"description\":\"There are now approximately 40,000 career Protestant missionaries who have gone from the United States to other parts of the world. Ten percent are from older “ ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.christianitytoday.com/1992/10/why-did-1800s-explode-with-missions/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"111\",\"title\":\"Christian Missionary Growth in the Nineteenth Century\",\"description\":\"Jun 17, 2009 · The number of Protestant foreign missionaries in the world grew from 100 missionaries in 1800 to over 21,000 missionaries by 1914. · The portion ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.rayfowler.org/2009/06/17/christian-missionary-growth-in-the-nineteenth-century/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"112\",\"title\":\"The Foreign Missionary Movement in the 19th and early 20th ...\",\"description\":\"In the last decades of the century, American missionary numbers increased substantially (to about 5,000 by 1900), and the major denominations all formed their ...Missing:  global expansion\",\"url\":\"https://nationalhumanitiescenter.org/tserve/nineteen/nkeyinfo/fmmovementb.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"113\",\"title\":\"20th Century Pentecostal and Evangelical Growth - Revival Library\",\"description\":\"Numerically it has become the largest new movement of evangelical history, reaching 550 million within 100 years of its genesis and by 2020 had risen to over ...\",\"url\":\"https://revival-library.org/histories/20th-century-pentecostal-and-evangelica