ice/the-anglican-reformation/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"136\",\"title\":\"The Anglican Church | World History - Lumen Learning\",\"description\":\"The English Reformation was associated with the wider process of the European Protestant Reformation, though based on Henry VIII's desire for an annulment of ...\",\"url\":\"https://courses.lumenlearning.com/suny-worldhistory/chapter/20-1-5-the-anglican-church/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"137\",\"title\":\"The 1559 Books of Common Prayer and the Elizabethan Reformation\",\"description\":\"Dec 18, 2015 · The 1559 Book of Common Prayer printed by Richard Jugge and John Cawood was the real thing that was authorised by the 1559 Act of Uniformity.\",\"url\":\"https://www.cambridge.org/core/journals/journal-of-ecclesiastical-history/article/1559-books-of-common-prayer-and-the-elizabethan-reformation/50333805D3C626BC4B61F2DE28C0DAA4\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"138\",\"title\":\"England's Return to Protestantism, 1559 - The History of Parliament\",\"description\":\"Jun 24, 2021 · In May 1559, six months after Elizabeth I ascended the throne, England formally returned to the Protestant fold, to the dismay of her Catholic bishops.\",\"url\":\"https://historyofparliament.com/2021/06/24/englands-return-to-protestantism-1559/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"139\",\"title\":\"Act of Uniformity 1559 - UK Parliament\",\"description\":\"A third Act of Uniformity (pictured) was passed in 1559, authorising a book of common prayer which was similar to the 1552 version but which retained some ...Missing:  settlement | Show results with:settlement\",\"url\":\"https://www.parliament.uk/about/living-heritage/transformingsociety/private-lives/religion/collections/common-prayer/act-of-uniformity-1559/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"140\",\"title\":\"[PDF] Thirty Nine Articles of Religion | Anglican Communion\",\"description\":\"Thirty Nine Articles of Religion. 1. Of Faith in the Holy Trinity ... The Romish Doctrine concerning Purgatory, Pardons, Worshipping and Adoration ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.anglicancommunion.org/media/109014/Thirty-Nine-Articles-of-Religion.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"141\",\"title\":\"Thirty-nine Articles of Religion (1571) - The Gospel Coalition\",\"description\":\"1. Of Faith in the Holy Trinity · 2. Of the Word or Son of God, Which Was Made Very Man · 3. Of the Going Down of Christ into Hell · 4. Of the Resurrection of ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thegospelcoalition.org/publication-online/thirty-nine-articles/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"142\",\"title\":\"Via Media - The Episcopal Church\",\"description\":\"Richard Hooker was the great apologist for the Elizabethan Settlement against both Puritanism and Roman Catholicism. Via media is often misunderstood in a ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.episcopalchurch.org/glossary/via-media/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"143\",\"title\":\"The Via Media—Between What and What?\",\"description\":\"May 17, 2020 · Richard Hooker, arguably the premier theologian of the English Reformation, clearly rejected this Protestant notion. His method was to read ...\",\"url\":\"https://northamanglican.com/the-via-media-between-what-and-what/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"144\",\"title\":\"Richard Hooker and the Via Media\",\"description\":\"The way of the English compromise has proved to be a hard way but there have been great men in the mould of Richard Hooker who have made the Anglican Way a real ...\",\"url\":\"https://mowatch.com.au/richard-hooker-and-the-via-media/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"145\",\"title\":\"WHO IS RICHARD HOOKER? - Earth and Altar\",\"description\":\"May 22, 2023 · Hooker to be the inventor of the via media (middle way) between “popery” and “puritanism” or between “Catholicism” and “Protestantism” that today we might call ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://earthandaltarmag.com/posts/omc4sdqt79ud6a3eyqe7sfbm44q2z5\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"146\",\"title\":\"Whatever happened to the Anglican Via Media?\",\"description\":\"Jan 30, 2018 · ... Richard Hooker (1544–1600) argued that Anglicanism retains the best of Roman Catholicism (liturgy and tradition) and Protestantism ...\",\"url\":\"https://anglicancompass.com/whatever-happened-to-the-anglican-via-media/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"147\",\"title\":\"Is Anglicanism Catholic or Protestant?\",\"description\":\"Sep 8, 2023 · Anglicanism is a kind of Reformed Catholicism, where Catholicism is the noun and Reformed is the adjective that modifies it.\",\"url\":\"https://northamanglican.com/is-anglicanism-catholic-or-protestant/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"148\",\"title\":\"The Via Media and the Muddled Middle - Three-Stream Living\",\"description\":\"Jan 20, 2015 · What Hooker was describing was a true third thing, a Reformation movement that took seriously the critiques of the Continental Reformers but at ...\",\"url\":\"https://threestreamliving.org/2015/01/20/the-via-media-and-the-muddled-middle/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"149\",\"title\":\"The Baptist Tradition - 500 Years of Reformations — and Their Books\",\"description\":\"Mar 28, 2023 · The first Baptist churches were formed by English-speakers in Holland (1609-1612). They believed, as did Martin Luther, that believers were capable of reading ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.missouristate.edu/Reformations/Baptist.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"150\",\"title\":\"Our History - ABCUSA\",\"description\":\"The earliest Baptist churches (1609-1612), although comprised of English- speaking congregants, flourished in Holland, where religious toleration was much ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.abc-usa.org/what-we-believe/our-history/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"151\",\"title\":\"Baptist Theology - The Gospel Coalition\",\"description\":\"Baptists believe in the Bible as the ultimate authority, a regenerate and baptized church, the autonomy of the local church, and religious liberty for all.\",\"url\":\"https://www.thegospelcoalition.org/essay/baptist-theology/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"152\",\"title\":\"Baptist Bible Study: History, Beliefs, Major Figures, and Resources\",\"description\":\"Dec 18, 2023 · Thomas Helwys (1575–1616), along with John Smyth, helped found the General Baptist movement and organized the first Baptist church. Roger ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.logos.com/grow/baptist-bible-study/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"153\",\"title\":\"Christian History Timeline: Baptists, 1600–2000\",\"description\":\"1612 Thomas Helwys forms the first Baptist church in London. 1638 Roger Williams forms the first Baptist congregation in America in Providence, Rhode Island.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://christianhistoryinstitute.org/magazine/article/christian-history-timeline-baptists-in-america\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"154\",\"title\":\"What Do Baptists Believe? An Intro to Baptist Theology \u0026 Roots\",\"description\":\"Sep 11, 2024 · Separation of church and state (disestablishmentarianism). This ... state and infant baptism required for both church membership and citizenship.\",\"url\":\"https://www.logos.com/grow/what-do-baptists-believe/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"155\",\"title\":\"Mission \u0026 History—Church-State Separation - BJC\",\"description\":\"Baptists became champions of religious liberty and church ... The Bible does not articulate a full-blown doctrine of the separation of church and state.\",\"url\":\"https://bjconline.org/mission-history-church-state-separation/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"156\",\"title\":\"Free church | Evangelical, Reformation \u0026 Revival - Britannica\",\"description\":\"Free church, generally, any Protestant religious body that exists in or originates in a land having a state church but that is itself free of governmental ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/topic/free-church-Protestantism\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"157\",\"title\":\"John Wesley and the History of Methodism - People.SMU\",\"description\":\"John Wesley's entrance into the Great Awakening began in November of 1729 at Pembroke College at Oxford. ... Only six years later, Wesley decided to sail to ...\",\"url\":\"https://people.smu.edu/mappingthega/stories/s15/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"158\",\"title\":\"John Wesley - Entry | Timelines | US Religion\",\"description\":\"In 1738, he experienced an evangelical conversion at a society meeting on Aldersgate Street, London, in which his “heart was strangely warmed.” This experience ...Missing:  key facts\",\"url\":\"https://www.thearda.com/us-religion/history/timelines/entry?etype=5\u0026eid=75\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"159\",\"title\":\"300th Anniversary of John Wesley's Birth - Louisiana UMC\",\"description\":\"The first Methodist Conference was held in 1744. Wesley would preside over 18 such conferences at Bristol. Wesley's travels took him across Great Britain and ...Missing:  key facts\",\"url\":\"https://www.la-umc.org/300thanniversaryofjohnwesleysbirth\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"160\",\"title\":\"Wesleyan Arminian | The best of all is, God is with us. -Wesley\",\"description\":\"Mar 30, 2025 · One of the cores of Arminian theology is that God wants everyone to be saved. Two passages that teach that are 1 Timothy 2:3-4, and 2 Peter 3:9.\",\"url\":\"https://wesleyanarminian.wordpress.com/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"161\",\"title\":\"A Sketch of a Biblical Theology of Sanctification: Wesleyan-Arminian ...\",\"description\":\"Oct 14, 2018 · We believe that sanctification is the work of God which transforms believers into the likeness of Christ. It is wrought by God's grace through ...\",\"url\":\"https://holyjoys.org/biblical-theology-sanctification/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"162\",\"title\":\"Statement of Faith - Asbury Theological Seminary\",\"description\":\"The following is a statement, in short form, of the Wesleyan-Arminian theological doctrines on which Asbury Theological Seminary was founded in 1923.\",\"url\":\"https://asburyseminary.edu/about/theological-orientation/statement-of-faith/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"163\",\"title\":\"History of the Holiness Movement\",\"description\":\"By the 1880s holiness was the most powerful doctrinal movement in America and seemed to be carrying away all opposition both within the Methodist Church and was ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.holinessmovement.org/history-of-the-holiness-movement/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"164\",\"title\":\"Holiness churches - World Council of Churches\",\"description\":\"The Holiness emphasis began taking on denominational expression with the founding of the Wesleyan Methodist Connection in 1843 and the Free Methodist Church in ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.oikoumene.org/church-families/holiness-churches\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"165\",\"title\":\"John Wesley | General Commission on Archives \u0026 History\",\"description\":\"English evangelical preacher, founder of Methodism, born in Epworth, Lincolnshire. He was ordained a deacon in the Church of England in 1725.Missing:  key facts\",\"url\":\"https://gcah.org/biographies/john-wesley/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"166\",\"title\":\"Wesleyan-Holiness Theology | www.asbury.edu\",\"description\":\"Wesley identified three doctrines in “A Short History of Methodism” (1765) that summed up the core of Methodist and Wesleyan-Holiness teaching.\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.asbury.edu/about/wesleyan-holiness-theology/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"167\",\"title\":\"United Methodist Collapse? - Juicy Ecumenism\",\"description\":\"Nov 25, 2024 · The United Methodist Church in the US lost 1.2 million members in 2023, or about 22 percent, the most that any denomination has ever lost in one year in ...\",\"url\":\"https://juicyecumenism.com/2024/11/25/united-methodist-collapse/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"168\",\"title\":\"Pentecostalism from soup to nuts: A (near) complete history of this ...\",\"description\":\"Feb 2, 2023 · Key to this movement are three dates: Jan. 1, 1901; April 3, 1960 and Feb. 18, 1967. Moder