ng - Timeline Event\",\"description\":\"He later publicly announced this event to the St. Mark's Episcopal Church in Van Nuys, California on April 3, 1960. While some parishioners supported Bennett, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.thearda.com/us-religion/history/timelines/entry?etype=1\u0026eid=219\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"175\",\"title\":\"Adventist Origins, Adventist History, Adventist Beliefs - Patheos\",\"description\":\"The Adventist Church grew out of the Millerite movement, which was based on the teachings of William Miller. Miller believed the Bible had within it coded dates ...Missing:  key | Show results with:key\",\"url\":\"https://www.patheos.com/library/adventist\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"176\",\"title\":\"Who are Seventh-day Adventists?\",\"description\":\"Many early Adventists came from Methodist backgrounds, and Adventist theology mirrors Methodist beliefs in many areas, including a rejection of Calvinistic ...Missing:  origins | Show results with:origins\",\"url\":\"https://uau.edu/adventists\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"177\",\"title\":\"Ellen G. White's contributions to the Seventh-day Adventist Church\",\"description\":\"God used Ellen White several times to steer the church through different crises. Although she died in 1915, her writings continue to guide the leadership of the ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.ministrymagazine.org/archive/2015/06/egw\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"178\",\"title\":\"Ellen G. White and Seventh-day Adventist Doctrines\",\"description\":\"Ellen White's role as a \\\"special messenger,\\\" vis-à-vis this doctrine, was largely that of validating the prior Biblical teaching of Miller, Joshua V. Himes, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.andrews.edu/~fortind/EGWDoctrines.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"179\",\"title\":\"Adventist Membership Tops 23 Million with Surge in Africa and PNG\",\"description\":\"May 14, 2025 · The Seventh-day Adventist Church has released the advance edition of its 2025 Annual Statistical Report, det