tschoolman.com/2013/12/20/on-moravians-and-other-radical-voices/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"213\",\"title\":\"Nikolaus Ludwig, count von Zinzendorf - Britannica\",\"description\":\"Zinzendorf's influence on church history was felt far beyond the boundaries of the Pietistic “heart religion” he had preached so fervently. Opposed equally to ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/biography/Nikolaus-Ludwig-Graf-von-Zinzendorf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"214\",\"title\":\"Great Awakening - First, Second \u0026 Definition | HISTORY\",\"description\":\"Mar 7, 2018 · The Great Awakening was a religious revival that impacted the English colonies in America during the 1730s and 1740s.\",\"url\":\"https://www.history.com/articles/great-awakening\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"215\",\"title\":\"Great Awakening | Definition, Summary, Key Figures, Significance ...\",\"description\":\"Oct 10, 2025 · Great Awakening, religious revival in the British American colonies between about 1720 and the 1740s. It was part of the religious ferment ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.britannica.com/event/Great-Awakening\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"216\",\"title\":\"1727 Great Awakening and Whitefield - Revival Library\",\"description\":\"Discover how the first Great Awakening was effectively the story of the Great Awakening and Whitefield, leaving a lasting impact on American religious life ...\",\"url\":\"https://revival-library.org/histories/1727-great-awakening-and-whitefield/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"217\",\"title\":\"Charles Finney's Rochester Revival - Entry | Timelines | US Religion\",\"description\":\"Evangelist Charles Grandison Finney held a powerful religious revival in Rochester, New York that lasted from September 1830 to March 1831.\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.thearda.com/us-religion/history/timelines/entry?etype=1\u0026eid=246\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"218\",\"title\":\"1824-1851 Charles Finney Revivals\",\"description\":\"A fi