yle, emphasizing the pulpit, communion table, and many windows. It includes adapted and new buildings, with styles ...\",\"url\":\"https://museeprotestant.org/en/notice/larchitecture-religieuse-protestante/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"262\",\"title\":\"The Protestant Reformation and Interior Church Architecture\",\"description\":\"The exhibition shows how the Protestant Reformation led to restricted religious images, and compares the Torgau Chapel with the Brussels Cathedral.\",\"url\":\"https://commons.case.edu/intersections-fa20/11/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"263\",\"title\":\"Bach and the Reformation - Christian Study Library\",\"description\":\"This article is on Johann Sebastian Bach and the influence Martin Luther and the Reformation had on him in his music and songs.\",\"url\":\"https://www.christianstudylibrary.org/article/bach-and-reformation\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"264\",\"title\":\"Without Luther, There Would Be No Bach - The Gospel Coalition\",\"description\":\"Mar 31, 2017 · Embodying a Lutheran theology of work, Bach viewed all of his music—whether sacred hymns or secular cantatas—as a calling from God. He ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.thegospelcoalition.org/article/without-luther-there-would-be-no-bach/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"265\",\"title\":\"J. S. Bach and the celebration of the Reformation | OUPblog\",\"description\":\"Oct 31, 2017 · It centers on Martin Luther's hymn, whose four verses appear in the work in various musical guises. It, too, invokes the theme of protection ...\",\"url\":\"https://blog.oup.com/2017/10/reformation-anniversary-bach/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"266\",\"title\":\"History of Work Ethic--4.Protestantism and the Protestant Ethic\",\"description\":\"He believed that people could serve God through their work, that the professions were useful, that work was the universal base of society and the cause of ...\",\"url\":\"http://workethic.coe.uga.edu/hpro.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\