r the Nicene Creed is a sign of its continuity with the early church. The decision to unilaterally revise ...\",\"url\":\"https://orthodoxbridge.com/category/filioque-clause/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"319\",\"title\":\"Defending the Filioque | Catholic Answers Magazine\",\"description\":\"The objections from the Orthodox can be broken into three categories. First, the claim is made that the filioque is a novelty of the ninth century that ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.catholic.com/magazine/print-edition/defending-the-filioque\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"320\",\"title\":\"Drop The Filioque .Com - Orthodox-Reformed Bridge\",\"description\":\"Sep 2, 2013 · If one applies the “filioque” to the ontological Trinity the result is that the Holy Spirit is treated as inferior to the Father and the Son and ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://orthodoxbridge.com/2013/09/02/drop-the-filioque-com/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"321\",\"title\":\"The Filioque Dispute | Eclectic Orthodoxy - WordPress.com\",\"description\":\"Aug 19, 2023 · It only gets serious if the Filioque is invoked in order to subordinate the Spirit to the Father and the Son—but no one advocates that! As the ...\",\"url\":\"https://afkimel.wordpress.com/2023/08/19/the-filioque-dispute/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"322\",\"title\":\"The Illogic of Calvin's Iconoclasm - Orthodox-Reformed Bridge\",\"description\":\"Feb 3, 2016 · Calvin's iconoclasm is illogical because he applied Old Testament rules anachronistically, his reasoning is flawed, and he misunderstood icons, ...\",\"url\":\"https://orthodoxbridge.com/2016/02/03/the-illogic-of-calvins-iconoclasm/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"323\",\"title\":\"The Icon FAQ - Orthodox Christian Information Center\",\"description\":\"Protestants might wish to take solace that at least Iconoclasts opposed the veneration of images, but veneration was never an issue per se with the Iconoclasts.\",\"url\":\"http://orthodoxinfo.com/general/icon_faq.aspx\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"324\",\"title\":\"A Short Guide to Iconoclasm in Early History - JSTOR Daily\",\"description\":\"Jan 28, 2015 · In the 8th century, the Eastern or Orthodox branch of Christianity gave history the word iconoclasm, from the Greek words for “icon smashing.”\",\"url\":\"https://daily.jstor.org/short-guide-iconoclasm-early-history/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"325\",\"title\":\"Icons and the Veneration of Saints - Orthodox-Reformed Bridge\",\"description\":\"Nov 2, 2011 · I've expanded my defense of the veneration of icons by discussing the different ontologies between the Reformed and Orthodox traditions.\",\"url\":\"https://orthodoxbridge.com/2011/11/02/icons-and-the-veneration-of-saints/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"326\",\"title\":\"Are Icons an Accretion? A Response to Gavin Ortlund\",\"description\":\"Aug 24, 2023 · Ortlund argues that icons are not a part of early Christianity but a later development or in his words an “accretion.”\",\"url\":\"https://orthodoxbridge.com/2023/08/24/are-icons-an-accretion-a-response-to-gavin-ortlund/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"327\",\"title\":\"Father, Son, and Controversy - Desiring God\",\"description\":\"Mar 23, 2020 · For the Orthodox, as the filioque controversy illustrates, the doctrine of the Trinity does not sit on the sidelines of faith. It is not merely ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.desiringgod.org/articles/father-son-and-controversy\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"328\",\"title\":\"Christian Ecumenism and Extravagant Mercy - Duke Divinity School\",\"description\":\"Mar 6, 2023 · The event most frequently credited with the launch of the ecumenical movement was the Edinburgh Missionary Conference of 1910. The call to unity ...\",\"url\":\"https://dukedivinity.medium.com/christian-ecumenism-and-extravagant-mercy-c11c4680352c\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"329\",\"title\":\"History | World Council of Churches\",\"description\":\"The 1937 Oxford Life and Work Conference, \\\"Church, Community and State\\\", approved a merger with Faith \u0026 Order that would form the World Council of Churches.\",\"url\":\"https://www.oikoumene.org/about-the-wcc/history\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"330\",\"title\":\"Evangelicals and Ecumenism - Christianity Today\",\"description\":\"Indeed, critics of the movement often accuse it of placing so much stress on visible unity that it compromises the prior importance of the truth. Some people ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.christianitytoday.com/1966/05/evangelicals-and-ecumenism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"331\",\"title\":\"1997 Joint Declaration on the Doctrine of Justification\",\"description\":\"The doctrine of justification was of central importance for the Lutheran Reformation of the sixteenth century. It was held to be the first and chief article.\",\"url\":\"https://www.christianunity.va/content/unitacristiani/en/dialoghi/sezione-occidentale/luterani/dialogo/documenti-di-dialogo/1999-dichiarazione-congiunta-sulla-dottrina-della-giustificazion/en.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"332\",\"title\":\"Joint Declaration on the Doctrine of Justification (JDDJ)\",\"description\":\"The Joint Declaration on the Doctrine of Justification (JDDJ) was a historic agreement signed by Lutherans and Catholics in 1999.\",\"url\":\"https://lutheranworld.org/what-we-do/unity-church/joint-declaration-doctrine-justification-jddj\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"333\",\"title\":\"The World Council of Churches - Musée protestant\",\"description\":\"The WCC stems mainly from Protestant youth and Church organisations who reflected on political and social challenges of the early 20th century in a world that ...\",\"url\":\"https://museeprotestant.org/en/notice/le-conseil-oecumenique-des-eglises/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"334\",\"title\":\"The Challenges of Ecumenism\",\"description\":\"Aug 29, 2017 · Ecumenism is the attempt to strengthen unity between the diverse Christian Churches through dialogue about doctrine, prayer in common, cooperation in good ...\",\"url\":\"https://ecumenism.net/2017/08/the-challenges-of-ecumenism.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"335\",\"title\":\"Challenges Facing the Ecumenical Movement in the 21st Century\",\"description\":\"Oct 22, 2005 · When we consider \\\"challenges\\\" facing the ecumenical movement today - as in any era - we may characterize them either as obstacles or as opportunities.\",\"url\":\"https://www.oikoumene.org/resources/documents/challenges-facing-the-ecumenical-movement-in-the-21st-century\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"336\",\"title\":\"Ecumenism: A Noble but Misguided Missionary Movement\",\"description\":\"Apr 6, 2024 · Ecumenism Doesn't Go Bad in a Vacuum​​ The blame for the theological compromises of the twentieth century does not entirely lie with ecumenism. ...\",\"url\":\"https://au.thegospelcoalition.org/article/ecumenicalism-a-noble-but-misguided-missionary-movement/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"337\",\"title\":\"The Problem with Ecumenism - Plain Bible Teaching\",\"description\":\"Feb 15, 2023 · Ecumenism is not the unity that is described in the New Testament. In fact, it is the type of union that the apostles repeatedly warned against throughout ...\u003c|control11|\u003e\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://plainbibleteaching.com/2023/02/15/the-problem-with-ecumenism/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"338\",\"title\":\"Protestantism - Missions And Expansion - Patheos\",\"description\":\"Protestant churches spread quickly in Europe, England, and America. When these regions became international powers, Protestant missionaries began to spread ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.patheos.com/library/protestantism/historical-development/missions-spread-changes-regional-adaptations\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"339\",\"title\":\"\",\"description\":\"\",\"url\":\"https://brill.com/downloadpdf/book/9789047441830/Bej.9789004170261.i-1004_006.pdf\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"340\",\"title\":\"Why Did the 1800s Explode with Missions | Christian History Magazine\",\"description\":\"There are now approximately 40,000 career Protestant missionaries who have gone from the United States to other parts of the world. Ten percent are from older ...Missing:  global | Show results with:global\",\"url\":\"https://christianhistoryinstitute.org/magazine/article/1800s-missions\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"341\",\"title\":\"The Foreign Missionary Movement in the 19th and early 20th ...\",\"description\":\"The foreign missionary movement gathered momentum. By 1900, its expansion was in full bloom, and would continue well into the twentieth century.\",\"url\":\"https://nationalhumanitiescenter.org/tserve/nineteen/nkeyinfo/fmmovement.htm\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"342\",\"title\":\"The missionary movement - Musée protestant\",\"description\":\"The missionary fervour of the Protestant Church arose in the nineteenth century. The first mission was in a country under the British rule.The pioneering age (1822-1884) · Origin of the missionary... · Bibliography\",\"url\":\"https://museeprotestant.org/en/notice/the-missionary-movement/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"343\",\"title\":\"Colonial expansion: missionaries between support and resistance\",\"description\":\"Nov 1, 2022 · In the 19th century, the first Protestant missionary societies emerged and sent out their workers. \\\"In this way, missionaries became ...Missing:  global | Show results with:global\",\"url\":\"https://www.mission-21.org/en/colonial-expansion-missionaries-intermediate-support-and-resistance/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"344\",\"title\":\"Evangelicalism and Westward Expansion in Early and Antebellum ...\",\"description\":\"Evangelical reformers and missionaries lent both institutional and ideological support to settler colonialism on Indigenous lands in the West. God's kingdom was ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.oah.org/tah/expansion/spreading-gods-kingdom-evangelicalism-and-westward-expansion-in-early-and-antebellum-america/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"345\",\"title\":\"2. Christian population change\",\"description\":\"Jun 9, 2025 · The number of Christians worldwide grew by 6%, from 2.1 billion in 2010 to 2.3 billion in 2020, while non-Christians grew by 15%.\",\"url\":\"https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2025/06/09/christian-population-change/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"346\",\"title\":\"How the Global Religious Landscape Changed From 2010 to 2020\",\"description\":\"Jun 9, 2025 · The number of Christians rose by 122 million, reaching 2.3 billion. · The number of Buddhists worldwide dropped by 19 million, declining to 324 ...2. Christian population change · Chapter 1 · 3. Muslim population change\",\"url\":\"https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2025/06/09/how-the-global-religious-landscape-changed-from-2010-to-2020/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"347\",\"title\":\"Religious identity in the United States | Pew Research Center\",\"description\":\"Feb 26, 2025 · Evangelicalism remains the largest tradition within Protestantism, but the evangelical share of the adult population also has ticked down, going ...\u003c|separator|\u003e\",\"url\":\"https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2025/02/26/religious-landscape-study-religious-identity/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"348\",\"title\":\"Protestants, Evangelicals, and Pentecostals to Represent Half of ...\",\"description\":\"By 2050, Protestants, including evangelicals and Pentecostals, are projected to represent roughly half of global Christians, with 1.48-1.60 billion adherents.\",\"url\":\"https://www.ccc.one/2025/08/protestants-evangelicals-and.html\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"349\",\"title\":\"Major Shift: Protestants Now Surpass Catholics in Attendance ...\",\"description\":\"Aug 19, 2025 · ... 2025, and poised to outnumber them in total adherents by 2050. In 2025, the worldwide Christian population stands at approximately 2.645 billion ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.wjbf.com/business/press-releases/ein-presswire/839480747/major-shift-protestants-now-surpass-catholics-in-attendance-worldwide-protestants-to-outnumber-catholics-before-2050\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"350\",\"title\":\"The Future of World Religions: Population Growth Projections, 2010 ...\",\"description\":\"Apr 2, 2015 · Europe's Christian population is expected to shrink by about 100 million people in the coming decades, dropping from 553 million to 454 million.Factors Driving Population... · Muslims · Christians · Hindus\",\"url\":\"https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2015/04/02/religious-projections-2010-2050/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"351\",\"title\":\"Pentecostals Will Be One Billion By 2050 - Dr. Palmer's Substack\",\"description\":\"Aug 3, 2025 · Pentecostals Will Be One Billion By 2050 · The Unstoppable Rise of Pentecostalism to One Billion Believers · If you are evangelical, mainline, ...\",\"url\":\"https://drchrispalmer.substack.com/p/pentecostals-will-be-one-billion\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"352\",\"title\":\"The Future Is Pentecostal - Influence Magazine\",\"description\":\"Aug 2, 2023 · Zurlo predicts that from 2020–50, Pentecostal and charismatic movements will still grow twice as fast as both the Christian and world populations.\",\"url\":\"https://influencemagazine.com/en/Practice/The-Future-Is-Pentecostal\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"353\",\"title\":\"9 Encouraging Trends for Global Christianity in 2025\",\"description\":\"Feb 11, 2025 · Christianity continues to grow around the world. Currently, there are more than 2.64 billion Christians. Christianity crossed the 2 billion mark this century.\",\"url\":\"https://research.lifeway.com/2025/02/11/9-encouraging-trends-for-global-christianity-in-2025/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"354\",\"title\":\"Global Christianity Surges Beyond Projections in 2024\",\"description\":\"Mar 15, 2024 · The Christian population is projected to climb from over 2.52 billion to 2.63 billion, representing a 1.08 percent growth, and is expected to surpass 3 billion ...Missing:  Research | Show results with:Research\",\"url\":\"https://www.frontierpartners.org/global-christianity-surges\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"355\",\"title\":\"Modeling the Future of Religion in America - Pew Research Center\",\"description\":\"Sep 13, 2022 · By 2055, the unaffiliated would make up the largest group (46%), ahead of Christians (43%). In 2070, 52% of Americans would be unaffiliated, ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.pewresearch.org/religion/2022/09/13/modeling-the-future-of-religion-in-america/\",\"favicon\":\"\"},{\"id\":\"356\",\"title\":\"Center for the Study of Global Christianity\",\"description\":\"The CSGC estimates a total of 5 million pastors/priests in all Christian traditions worldwide (Catholics, Orthodox, Protestants, and Independents, including bi- ...\",\"url\":\"https://www.gordonconwell.edu/center-for-global-christianity/research/quick-facts/\",\"favicon\":\"\"}],\"images\":[{\"id\":\"99f4f7ff45f1\",\"caption\":\"Martin Luther's Ninety-Five Theses\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/95Thesen_facsimile_colour.png\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"c7e0a995d1ae\",\"caption\":\"Latin version of the Christian cross which is used by virtually all Protestant denominations\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Golden_Christian_Cross.svg.png\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"bd5193b6ba36\",\"caption\":\"Luther's translation of the Bible into German\",\"url\":\"._assets_/Lutherbibel.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"cfb3ca06463b\",\"caption\":\"Last Supper depiction from Lutheran context\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Abendmahl-1547-LC.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"4a77127663d4\",\"caption\":\"Jan Hus at the Council of Constance\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/Muttich%252C_Kamil_Vladislav_-_Mistr_Jan_Hus_na_hranici_v_Kostnici_1415.jpg\",\"position\":\"CENTER\",\"width\":0,\"height\":0},{\"id\":\"99f4f7ff45f1\",\"caption\":\"Facsimile of Martin Luther's Ninety-five Theses\",\"url\":\"./_assets_/95Thesen_facsimile_colour.png